title: $:/lithic/styles/pyramid.css
tags: $:/tags/Stylesheet
type: text/css

/*
Pyramid sidebar ($:/lithic/ui/SideBar/Pyramid): converts the active nodestream
into a mermaid tree and marks the node mirroring the tiddler currently being
edited with the `activeStyle` class (see the macro's `:::activeStyle` hints).

pele keeps those class names on each node group (g.pele-node.activeStyle), so
the active node is styled by class and inherits the palette theme for everything
else. Only the active node needs special handling here.

This sheet is text/css: TW's wikitext stylesheet parser rewrites the
--lithic-c-* double hyphens into en-dashes inside text/vnd.tiddlywiki sheets.
*/

/* Active node fill/border = accent pair (accent-fg is derived >= 4.5:1 on accent) */
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) .pele-node.activeStyle :is(rect, path, polygon, circle, ellipse) {
    fill: var(--lithic-c-accent) !important;
    stroke: var(--lithic-c-accent-fg) !important;
    stroke-width: 2px !important;
}

/* Active node label keeps the derived accent foreground */
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) .pele-node.activeStyle text,
div.mm-themed:not(.mm-user) .pele-node.activeStyle tspan {
    fill: var(--lithic-c-accent-fg) !important;
    font-weight: bold !important;
}